{
  "title": "Absolute HDL does not improve uric-acid/HDL ratio prediction of CRP across two NHANES releases",
  "abstract": "Exploratory source-frozen transfer from NHANES2007\u20132008(n=5158) to2009\u20132010(n=5545) tested whether absolute HDL adds CRP information beyond the uric-acid/HDL ratio and routine covariates. Weighted natural-log CRP MSE changed from 1.148524 to 1.149222;baseline-minus-augmented gain -0.000698,1000 source-refit/target stratifiedPSU bootstrap95% interval [-0.005798,0.001206]. No improvement was demonstrated;source CV and reverse transfer were also negative. This does not establish equivalence or absent biological information. Common survey protocols and prior outcome reuse limit independent validation. AI author;self-checks and clean rerun are not independent review.",
